      "page_level_design_instruction": "The Home page for Courtside & Crown is the definitive first impression of a century-old tennis institution. Every design decision must reinforce the heritage_classic aesthetic \u2014 formal, prestigious, warm, and storied \u2014 while maintaining the clarity and navigability expected of a modern card-grid layout family.\n\n**Overall Page Rhythm & Section Sequencing:**\nThe page flows through five distinct sections with deliberate tonal shifts: (1) a commanding full-viewport hero that anchors prestige, (2) a tight horizontal stats band that delivers authority through numbers, (3) a three-column feature card grid that communicates the academy's core pillars, (4) a testimonial card row that introduces human warmth and social proof, and (5) a richly textured full-width CTA close. This arc moves from grandiose establishment \u2192 credibility \u2192 clarity of offering \u2192 emotional resonance \u2192 conversion. Each section transition uses a subtle ornamental rule or a tonal background shift to create breathing room without breaking the formal register.\n\n**Background & Color Rhythm:**\nSections alternate between Crown Ivory (#F5F0E8) and Antique Linen (#EAE3D2) backgrounds to create gentle layered depth without sharp contrast breaks. The hero and CTA sections use Courtside Navy (#1B2A4A) as the dominant dark surface, bookending the page with gravitas. Championship Gold (#B8962E) is used sparingly as a decorative accent \u2014 ornamental dividers, rule lines, badge borders \u2014 never as a background fill. Burgundy Crest (#7D1D3F) drives all primary CTAs, active states, and key highlight moments. Forest Court (#2D5016) appears only in category tags and incidental squad indicators. Slate Mist (#D6D9E0) handles all card borders and divider lines.\n\n**Typography Hierarchy:**\nAll headings are set in Playfair Display \u2014 H1 at a commanding display scale (clamp between 52px\u201380px), H2 at 36\u201348px, H3 at 24\u201330px \u2014 with tight letter-spacing at large sizes and sentence case throughout. Eyebrow labels use Montserrat in uppercase small caps with wide letter-spacing (0.15\u20130.2em), set in Championship Gold or Burgundy Crest depending on background darkness. Body and descriptive copy uses Source Serif 4 at 17\u201318px with 1.7 line height. Stat figures and metadata use Montserrat uppercase, bold, at oversized display scale. Card metadata and captions use Montserrat at 11\u201312px, Ink Smoke (#4A4E5A).\n\n**Layout Grid & Density:**\nThe page uses a 12-column grid with a max content width of 1280px, centered with generous horizontal padding (80px desktop, 40px tablet, 20px mobile). Sections maintain vertical padding of 96px top/bottom on desktop, scaling to 64px on tablet and 48px on mobile. The card grid sections use a 3-column layout on desktop, 2-column on tablet, and 1-column on mobile, with 28px gutters. Cards have 32px internal padding, rounded corners at 4px (restrained, not modern-bubbly), and a 1px Slate Mist border with a subtle box shadow (0 2px 12px rgba(27,42,74,0.08)) for elevation.\n\n**Visual Motifs & Ornamental Language:**\nSymmetrical composition is enforced wherever possible \u2014 centered section headers, balanced two-CTA arrangements, evenly spaced card grids. Ornamental dividers (thin horizontal rules flanked by small diamond or lozenge marks in Championship Gold) separate eyebrow labels from headlines in major sections. Crest-like marks and the central emblem illustration in the hero reinforce the heraldic vocabulary. No rounded pill buttons \u2014 CTAs use rectangular buttons with 2px solid borders, either filled (Burgundy Crest background, Crown Ivory text) or outlined (Crown Ivory border, Crown Ivory text on dark backgrounds).\n\n**Responsive Behavior:**\nOn mobile, the hero stacks vertically with the emblem illustration centered above the headline. Stat items stack to a 2\u00d72 grid then single column. Feature cards and testimonial cards become single-column scrollable stacks. The CTA section maintains its textured background but reduces padding; both CTA buttons stack vertically and expand to full width. Navigation collapses to a hamburger menu that slides in from the right with a Courtside Navy overlay.\n\n**Fit Within the Shared Design System:**\nThis page establishes the visual language that all subsequent pages inherit. The hero's emblem, the gold ornamental dividers, the Playfair Display headline scale, and the Burgundy Crest CTA button style must be treated as the canonical reference for the entire site. The page demonstrates the full color palette in use, introduces all three typefaces in their correct roles, and validates the card-grid layout family as the primary structural pattern.",
